{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>It is a guilt-offering, it is a guilt-offering, a guilt-offering.</b> The first is entirely with qamatz — it is a noun; and the last is half qamatz and half patach — it is a verb form. And if you should say the verse is unnecessary — it has already been expounded in Torat Kohanim: <b>אָשָׁם אָשָׁם</b> — to bring the guilt-offering of a betrothed maidservant, that it must be a ram worth two shekels. One might think I include the guilt-offering of a nazirite and the guilt-offering of a leper — Scripture says הוא (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:06.650070886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}